      "body": {
        "text": "Your baby doesn’t need teeth to eat real food! 🍍\n\nWondering what foods your 6-month-old baby can eat? You might be surprised by how many options you have. \n\nFrom steak and chicken to pasta, broccoli, and pineapple, babies can explore a wide variety of flavours and textures from around 6 months old. \n\nThe key isn’t how many teeth your baby has — it’s whether they’re showing signs of readiness for starting solids and whether food is prepared safely for their age and developmental stage.\n\n5 foods your baby can explore from 6 months:\n\n🥩 Steak\n🍝 Pasta\n🍗 Chicken\n🥦 Broccoli\n🍍 Pineapple\n\nRemember: Every baby develops at their own pace. Always check for readiness signs, offer appropriately prepared foods, and supervise your baby while eating.\n\n🔎 Search hundreds of foods in the Solid Starts app\n\n📲 SHARE with a parent who’s getting ready to start solids!\n\nFollow @solidstarts for more baby-led weaning tips, first foods inspiration, and practical advice for introducing solids with confidence. 🤍\n\n#StartingSolids #BabyLedWeaning #BLW #BabyFirstFoods #6MonthOldBaby"
      },
